            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary vascular reserve in heart transplantation. Normalization after therapy for rejection].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2053-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute rejection is associated with severe impairment of coronary reserve in heart transplants. To evaluate the effects of rejection therapy, coronary reserve was assessed in 6 patients before and after treatment of an acute episode of rejection. Coronary reserve was significantly enhanced after rejection therapy (4.7 +/- 0.8, vs 2.3 +/- 0.5, P less than 0.001) and was not significantly different from that of transplanted patients without rejection (5.4 +/- 0.8). This study provides evidence that alterations of coronary reserve due to acute rejection are reversible after treatment of the rejection episode.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
